{"id": "EUVD-2026-103808", "enisaUuid": "3f81e451-8365-3f23-bf68-cf01712cb91c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-pcache: reject a kset that overruns its segment\n\ncache_replay(), the writeback worker and the GC worker read a kset of\nget_kset_onmedia_size() bytes and advance the position by it. A forged\nkey_num makes that size exceed the segment's remaining space, so the\nadvance walks past the segment and trips the cache_pos_advance() BUG_ON.\n\nReject a kset whose on-media size exceeds cache_seg_remain() before use.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:27:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01a700e9278da5706c865b9ca3ae70fdb7b4531d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96e2863b1f81ea61b8d8d5d5a45d3b4c018f8e10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ac1f10f987a2ffae4aecf0e2ceca8f552b665cb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98868", "GHSA-94mx-pc7x-6h6x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "246c0cd6-3778-3b60-94d1-8d098e6621a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "3a50502d-2172-3b8c-914e-f247a8cbfe4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "3acb1fcd-3ac5-3ee7-a3e7-2165ba9c87da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "9b0887e1-04ce-35c2-bfbe-2bfe8c349100", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <7ac1f10f987a2ffae4aecf0e2ceca8f552b665cb"}, {"id": "c922b1ae-97be-3a2b-ab63-2fbd6e2439d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ca4b8c6f-b4ca-30ef-a088-71eea467f0c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ea5115d0-8519-3624-bddc-4f094299ab26", "product"